# ## CRITICAL: Long-File Write Protocol (Cline CLI platform limit)
# The `editor` tool truncates large writes (~5000-6000 chars). Use shell writes instead:
#
# 1. Literal content you already have:
#      cat > /path/file << 'EOF'
#      ...content...
#      EOF
#    (single-quoted delimiter — no shell expansion)
# 2. Generated content:  python3 -c "print(...)" | cat > /path/file
# 3. Very large / complex: python3 << 'PYEOF' ... with open(f,'w') as fh: fh.write(...) PYEOF
# 4. Long literal (>10k chars): write in chunks with `>>` (append)
#
# Rules:
# - ALWAYS single-quote the heredoc delimiter ('EOF')
# - Files >10KB: build in 3-4 sequential `cat >>` chunks, then verify
# - Never `tee`/`>` INSIDE a heredoc (they become literal text)
# - For generated content use the PIPE form, not heredoc with $(...)  (a quoted heredoc
#   writes literal `$(...)`; an unquoted one explodes into "File name too long")
# - ALWAYS verify after writing:  wc -l file && head -3 file && tail -3 file
# - "unexpected EOF" = missing/mismatched delimiter
# - **Batch config/prose edits**: apply as (old→new) pairs with per-pattern count assertions and
#   write ONLY if every pattern matched (all-or-nothing). This caught 3 would-be YAML
#   corruptions on 2026-09-20. Validate YAML after every .yaml/.yml write; never YAML-validate
#   a Markdown file (it aborts the write).
# - **Verify sequentially, not in the same batch as the write** — parallel write+grep yields
#   false "still stale" readings.
#
# ## DAILY WORKFLOW
#
# ### Before starting
# 1. Read the handoff (`data/coordination/CLINE_TO_MAKALI_DEBUT_SWEEP_BRIEFING_20260920.md`) +
#    `OMEGA_ENGINE.md` + `data/coordination/ACTIVE_SPRINT.json`
# 2. `git log --oneline -5 && git status --short | wc -l` (the tree is usually dirty — know whose
#    work is whose; NEVER `git add -A`)
# 3. Baseline: `make check-mandates` + focused `pytest` on the area you will touch
# 4. `hivemind_get_awareness()` — who else is active?
# 5. Parallel agent work? → `hivemind_post_context(channel="cline", entity="omega-engine", ...)`
#
# ### During work
# - Writes >4000 chars: heredoc via `run_commands`, not `editor`
# - Shell: `source .venv/bin/activate` — NEVER `--break-system-packages` (M24)
# - Heartbeat every 5-10 min: `hivemind_heartbeat(channel="cline", entity="omega-engine")`
# - **Before committing**: `make check-mandates`, focused `pytest`, and a scoped `git add` of
#   explicit paths (`git restore --staged` anything that is not yours first)
# - Commit prefixes: `feat:|fix:|docs:|refactor:|test:|ci:|chore:`
# - Push: `git push origin release/debut-v1.6.0`
#
# ### After session
# - Distill L1→L2→L3 to `proposed_lessons.yaml` (M11) — blind staging, never straight into soul.yaml
# - Post completion: `hivemind_post_context(intent="status", ...)`
# - If you regenerated anything generated, re-check the gates that depend on it (see M13 caveat)
#
# ### TEST TRUTH (verify, never quote a count blindly)
# - CI authority = the `Test` workflow: `python3 -m pytest tests/ -v --tb=short -x`
#   Latest measured (job 3.13, run 35496559076, HEAD 70291e94): **2008 tests in 138.72s**
#   → 90 skipped, 4 expected failures. Counts shift with early-stop/xdist batching.
# - `pyproject.toml [tool.pytest.ini_options]` addopts =
#   "-n auto -x --tb=short --ignore=data/entities/roc_racoon/workspace/odysseus-dev
#    --timeout=60 --durations=15"  ⇒ pytest-xdist is ALWAYS on, so **`-x` is not final**:
#   workers finish in-flight tests, and one run can report several failures/errors at once.
# - Local full-suite runs are unstable on the 14Gi dev box (OOM risk) — CI is the authority.
# - Prefer targeted runs: `make test-debug TEST=<pattern>`, `make test`, `make test-all`
# - Historical claims (681 / 855 / 1315 / 1654 / 2208 tests) are STALE — do not reuse them
# - `make test` takes NO `ARGS=` passthrough (it is `pytest -x --tb=short -m "not integration"`)
