# ## ERROR RECOVERY PROTOCOLS
# Standard: read the stack → `git diff HEAD` → run the specific test → fix forward (never revert
#   without understanding root cause) → `make check-mandates` + focused pytest.
# Compaction: handoff briefing → `OMEGA_ENGINE.md` → `SOVEREIGN_MANDATES.md` → `PIVOT_LOG.md` →
#   `make check-mandates` → `make codex` if M13 is red → `.opencode/anchored-summary.md`.
# Hivemind: `curl -s http://127.0.0.1:8016/health` → `cline config mcp --json` (5 servers) →
#   `cd mcp_servers/omega_hub && python server.py`.
# Lifeboat: `git stash` / restore `config/omega.yaml` template / `git bisect` / fresh clone to /tmp.
# **CI red?** Read the failing STEP first (`gh run view <id> --json jobs`), then the log:
#   `gh run view <id> --log-failed | sed 's/^[^ ]*Z //' | tail -40`. A missing tool (ruff, rg) is an
#   install problem, not a code problem. Never conclude "tests fail" without naming the test.
