# ## §TRAPS DISCOVERED (deep-dive 2026-09-20 — do not repeat)
# 1. **Blanket `*.md` ignore (`.gitignore:270`).** New markdown silently never enters the repo;
#    README/CONTRIBUTING only exist because they predate the rule. After creating ANY doc run
#    `git ls-files --error-unmatch <file>`. A LATER `*.md` rule OVERRIDES an earlier `!` negation,
#    so negatives must sit AFTER it (fixed 2026-09-20: `!data/coordination/CLINE_*.md`,
#    `!QUICKSTART.md`, `!SECURITY.md`, `!CHANGELOG.md`, `!docs/USER_MANUAL.md`, `!docs/user/*.md`).
# 2. **Hardcoded absolute paths in tests.** `tests/jem/test_dispatch_guard_adversarial.py:435`
#    carried `dir="/home/arcana-novai/..."` -> FileNotFoundError on every other checkout (CI).
#    Always derive root: `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent`. Audit before pushing:
#    `grep -rn 'arcana-novai\|/Users/' tests/ --include='*.py'`
# 3. **Tests passing only because of dirty local state.** `test_first_breath_recording` passed
#    locally for months off a stale `data/memory/entity_births.db` row (2026-06-13) while the
#    feature was unwired dead code (D-605). Locally-green/CI-red => suspect UNTRACKED state first.
# 4. **Dual module identity (`src.omega.*` vs `omega.*`).** The same file loads twice, so patching
#    `omega.astrology.X` does NOT affect `src.omega.astrology.X`. Import one way only, everywhere.
# 5. **Generated artifacts can depend on untracked sources.** `make codex` reads `ORACLE_STACK.md`,
#    `CREDITS.md`, `scripts/codex/*.md`, `docs/kb/REFINEMENT_PROTOCOL.md` (list: `scripts/groups.json`).
#    When you add a generator, check its source list for ignore coverage.
# 6. **REUSE sidecar trap.** Untracking `X.backup.license` orphans `X.backup` -> REUSE v3.3 fails on
#    the parent. Ignore/untrack BOTH `*.backup.*` AND bare `*.backup`.
# 7. **Time-dependent gates.** M13 is a freshness property, not a code property. Never pin its
#    number without the "`make codex` refreshes it" caveat.
# 8. **`-x` is not final under pytest-xdist** (`-n auto` is in addopts): one run can report several
#    failures, so a "single" red is often a cluster. Also, a matrix sibling CANCELED by fail-fast is
#    a SYMPTOM of the other version failing — read the triager before believing a second cause.
# 9. **All-or-nothing batch edits.** Assert every (old -> new) pattern matches; abort WITHOUT writing
#    if any miss. Never YAML-validate a Markdown file (it aborts the write).
# 10. **Parallel write+verify races.** Writing and grepping the same file in one batch yields false
#     "still stale" readings. Verify sequentially.
# 11. **Stale counts + split sentences.** 681/855/1315/1654/2208 test claims are ALL superseded —
#     measure. And re-grep prose after multi-pass edits (a sweep + a block replace split a sentence).
#
